From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muhammad Falak R Wani <falakreyaz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:39:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vendor: encode cgroups device filter without cilium asm

Port the opencontainers/cgroups device-filter encoder change into the cgroups source vendored by runc 1.5.2. The filter uses only a small, fixed subset of single-width BPF instructions, so keep its encoding local and resolve each rule branch directly. This removes the runtime import of cilium/ebpf/asm and its crypto dependencies without changing emitted instructions.

The corresponding cgroups change and decoder tests are in the separate upstream patch series (mfrw/devices-no-go-crypto). This vendor patch omits tests because upstream dist-git vendor archives do not include test files.
---
